# GLO's Tempo page: after Mix; KNOB 1 the tempo; any key taps it in quarter notes (two
# taps make a tempo, then the mean of the last four gaps, in whole BPM); bounces and keys together ignored; two seconds quiet, a
# load, the knob or leaving the page start again; the keys play, write and record nothing; playing keeps its place;
# a MIDI clock in leads (its tempo shown, the stored one untouched by the page)
wait 300
projnew
expect filled1 0
expect filled2 0
tap GLO
expect page Mix
turn SELECT 1
expect page Tempo
wait 40
shot tempo.png
expect tempo10 1200
expect taps 0

# KNOB 1: whole BPM, HOME held tenths (its release opens no page), 40 to 220
spin K1 5
expect tempo10 1250
press HOME
spin K1 -3
release HOME
wait 20
expect page Tempo
expect tempo10 1247
spin K1 -200
expect tempo10 400
spin K1 300
expect tempo10 2200
bpm 100
expect tempo10 1000

# two taps 500 ms apart: 120 (a tapkey is 90 ms: then 410 more); the first alone changes nothing
tapkey w0
expect taps 1
expect tempo10 1000
shot tempo_pulse.png
wait 410
tapkey b3
expect taps 2
expect tempo10 1200
wait 410
tapkey w5
expect tempo10 1200
# a gap of 520: the mean of 500 500 520 (118.4: whole BPM, 118)
wait 430
tapkey w9
expect tempo10 1180
# the last four gaps only: 500 520 500 500 (118.8: 119), then the 520 drops out after four more 500s
wait 410
tapkey w1
expect tempo10 1190
wait 410
tapkey w1
wait 410
tapkey w1
expect tempo10 1190
wait 410
tapkey w1
expect tempo10 1200
expect taps 8
wait 40
shot tempo_taps.png

# a gap far off the mean (300 ms): a new tempo at once, from that gap (200)
wait 170
tapkey w0
expect tempo10 2000
expect taps 2
wait 210
tapkey w0
expect tempo10 2000
expect taps 3

# a bounce (the same key 30 ms later) and two keys at once: one tap
wait 210
key w2 down
key w2 up
wait 30
key w2 down
key w2 up
key w3 down
key w4 down
key w3 up
key w4 up
expect taps 4
expect tempo10 2000

# two seconds without a tap: the next one starts again (alone it changes nothing)
wait 2100
expect taps 0
tapkey w0
expect taps 1
expect tempo10 2000
# a gap past either end gives that end: 1800 ms (33 BPM) -> 40, then 200 ms (300 BPM) -> 220
wait 1710
tapkey w0
expect tempo10 400
wait 2100
tapkey w0
wait 110
tapkey w0
expect tempo10 2200

# the knob, leaving the page, HOME held, a new project: the taps start again
bpm 120
tapkey w0
expect taps 1
spin K1 1
expect taps 0
expect tempo10 1210
tapkey w0
expect taps 1
turn SELECT 1
wait 40
expect page Master_EQ
expect taps 0
turn SELECT -1
expect page Tempo
press HOME
tapkey w0
release HOME
wait 20
expect taps 0
expect page Tempo
tapkey w0
expect taps 1
projnew
wait 40
expect taps 0
expect tempo10 1200
expect page Tempo

# the keys play nothing (a kit on T1, a synth on T2) and write nothing, step record armed too
expect voices 0
expect drumhits 0
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 2
tapkey w0
wait 410
tapkey w4
wait 40
expect voices 0
expect drumhits 0
tap REC
wait 40
shot tempo_steprec.png
tapkey w0
wait 410
tapkey b1
expect filled1 0
expect filled2 0
expect voices 0
expect tempo10 1200
tap REC

# playing: a tap changes the rate, never the place (no restart: the sixteenths go on counting)
tap PLAY
wait 1000
expect playing 1
expect six >6
tapkey w0
wait 310
tapkey w0
wait 310
tapkey w0
expect tempo10 1500
expect playing 1
expect six >13
wait 800
expect six >18
# REC held while playing: the keys still only tap, nothing recorded (and REC held starts no recording here)
press REC
tapkey w0
wait 310
tapkey w2
wait 310
tapkey b0
wait 40
shot tempo_rec_held.png
release REC
expect tempo10 1500
wait 1000
expect filled1 0
expect filled2 0
# live recording latched (REC + PLAY): still only taps
tap PLAY
wait 40
press REC
tap PLAY
release REC
wait 300
tapkey w0
wait 410
tapkey w6
wait 410
tapkey b4
expect tempo10 1200
wait 1500
tap PLAY
wait 40
expect filled1 0
expect filled2 0
expect playing 0

# a MIDI clock in leads: its tempo shown and followed; the taps and KNOB 1 leave the stored tempo as it is
bpm 100
clock 24 20
expect ext 1
expect tempo >122
expect tempo <128
wait 10
shot tempo_ext.png
tapkey w0
clock 20 20
tapkey w0
clock 20 20
tapkey w0
expect taps 0
expect tempo10 1000
spin K1 5
expect tempo10 1000
clock 10 20
expect ext 1
# the clock gone (half a second): LOOM-8's own again, the taps count
wait 700
expect ext 0
expect tempo 100
tapkey w0
wait 410
tapkey w0
expect tempo10 1200

# the screen reader: the page, its hint; a tap's new tempo said as KNOB 1's value (600 ms: 100)
wait 2100
listen
where
said Tempo, page 2 of 8
where
said keys: tap
tapkey w0
wait 510
tapkey w0
wait 300
said TEMPO 100.0
